<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dimapur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dimapur is the largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagaland">Nagaland</a> in north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the Dhansiri river. It was the capital of the Dimasa <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dimasa-kingdom">Kachari kingdom</a> until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahom-people">Ahoms</a> sacked it in 1536. The ruins of the old city include a brick gateway and groups of carved stone pillars with mushroom-shaped tops. It is now the main commercial and transport hub of Nagaland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dimapur.jpg" alt="Dimapur" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PP Yoonus · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dimapur_Town.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
